tps://api.github.com/users/GlitchedCode922/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlitchedCode922/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlitchedCode922/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlitchedCode922/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlitchedCode922/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-18T16:31:15Z","updated_at":"2025-02-19T14:17:46Z","body":"Also having this issue. For me, it also reproduced on virtual Linux in proot-distro with Godot 4.2","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2666231920/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2667320452","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101007#issuecomment-2667320452","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101007","id":2667320452,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6e_BSE","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-19T01:51:05Z","updated_at":"2025-02-20T02:50:12Z","body":"On Android the `get_modified_time` function doesn’t work properly; ~~after saving the time is the same.~~\nAfter saving, the timestamp of the file is adjusted correctly, but is reset before export.\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/e948f52ea93cfff23b4a24b83d310724be2fb208/editor/export/editor_export_platform.cpp#L814-L819\n\n\nWhen the project is saved, the following warnings are displayed in the logcat. I'll try to continue debugging in the next few days.\n\n```sh\n2025-02-19 02:35:56.960  1560-2230  MediaProvider           com...ndroid.providers.media.module  W  Database update failed while renaming /storage/emulated/0/Documents/bug_101007_repro-godotatoaexportedcache/control.tscn-IfbFhZ (Ask Gemini)\n                                                                                                    android.database.sqlite.SQLiteConstraintException: UNIQUE constraint failed: files._data (code 2067 SQLITE_CONSTRAINT_UNIQUE)\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2667320452/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"outdated"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2670335154","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101007#issuecomment-2670335154","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101007","id":2670335154,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fKhSy","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-20T02:50:00Z","updated_at":"2025-02-20T02:55:21Z","body":"--> https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/thirdparty/minizip/unzip.c\n\n-----------\n\nThe timestamp (`modified_time`) of the scene file is reset (perhaps other project files are also affected). Whenever the file `libgodot_android.so` is processed. (25 MB)\n\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/70eb62faf24223f1dcf90589f4b39d1be7609ca0/platform/android/export/export_plugin.cpp#L3652\n\nDuring the first export, the timestamp of the scene file is only reset at the end of the function (not always):\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/70eb62faf24223f1dcf90589f4b39d1be7609ca0/platform/android/export/export_plugin.cpp#L3899\n\n----------\n\nAs a test, I skipped the `libgodot_android.so` file during export. The timestamp of the scene file was no longer changed. Of course, the exported APK file is unusable without the .so file.\n\n@akien-mga \nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blame/master/thirdparty/minizip/patches/0001-godot-seek.patch\n\nI discovered this patch file in the folder, last updated about two years ago with bug fixes, etc. Should we try a new version first? We can also add a workaround on Android (e.g. the `created timestamp` will also change after saving but will not be reset when exporting).\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2670335154/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2670752885","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101007#issuecomment-2670752885","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101007","id":2670752885,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fMHR1","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-20T08:11:47Z","updated_at":"2025-02-20T08:11:47Z","body":"@Alex2782 We're very close to the 4.4 release, so it would be safer to implement a workaround for Android for now. We can refine it in 4.5.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2670752885/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2675177510","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101007#issuecomment-2675177510","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101007","id":2675177510,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fc_gm","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-21T17:43:00Z","updated_at":"2025-02-21T17:43:00Z","body":"> --> https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/thirdparty/minizip/unzip.c\n> \n> -----------\n> \n> The timestamp (`modified_time`) of the scene file is reset (perhaps other project files are also affected). Whenever the file `libgodot_android.so` is processed. (25 MB)\n> \n> \n> https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/70eb62faf24223f1dcf90589f4b39d1be7609ca0/platform/android/export/export_plugin.cpp#L3652\n> \n> During the first export, the timestamp of the scene file is only reset at the end of the function (not always):\n> https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/70eb62faf24223f1dcf90589f4b39d1be7609ca0/platform/android/export/export_plugin.cpp#L3899\n> \n> ----------\n> \n> As a test, I skipped the `libgodot_android.so` file during export. The timestamp of the scene file was no longer changed. Of course, the exported APK file is unusable without the .so file.\n> \n> @akien-mga \n> https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blame/master/thirdparty/minizip/patches/0001-godot-seek.patch\n> \n> I discovered this patch file in the folder, last updated about two years ago with bug fixes, etc. Should we try a new version first? We can also add a workaround on Android (e.g. the `created timestamp` will also change after saving but will not be reset when exporting).\n> \n\n@Alex2782 let's make sure we have an entry in the Android project tracker to properly address the issue in Godot 4.5.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2675177510/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2675758282","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101007#issuecomment-2675758282","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101007","id":2675758282,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ffNTK","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-21T22:37:02Z","updated_at":"2025-02-22T00:31:25Z","body":"On [Android Tracker](https://github.com/orgs/godotengine/projects/110/views/1) as a `Draft`\n\n------------\n\nI currently have no ideas as to what could be causing this mysterious behavior. Even without export and even if Godot Editor was not active, the timestamp of the file (only `modified_time`) was reset.\n\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103080#issue-2866593827\n\n>After saving, all timestamps (st_mtime, st_ctime, st_atime) are set to the same value.\nAfter exporting or after some time, only modified_time resets to a past timestamp.\n....\nI initially suspected thirdparty/minizip/unzip.c because the timestamps were only reset after unz* functions. However, this behavior also occurs when no export is performed, once even when the Godot Editor was not running (terminated).\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2675758282/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2675911718","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101007#issuecomment-2675911718","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101007","id":2675911718,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ffywm","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-22T01:17:57Z","updated_at":"2025-02-22T01:17:57Z","body":"@Alex2782 I ran into a similar issue when investigating https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/94416. See  https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/94416#issuecomment-2267172619 \n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2675911718/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2675924557","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101007#issuecomment-2675924557","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101007","id":2675924557,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ff15N","user":{"login":"Alex2782","id":41921395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTIxMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41921395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782","html_url":"https://github.com/Alex2782","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Alex2782/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-22T01:39:42Z","updated_at":"2025-02-22T01:39:42Z","body":"> Also having this issue. For me, it also reproduced on virtual Linux in proot-distro with Godot 4.2\n\n@GlitchedCode922 Did you save the project files on a partition with `lazytime`?\n\n`mount | grep 'lazytime'` \n\n`proot-distro`? that? -> https://wiki.termux.com/wiki/PRoot\n\n-------------\nhttps://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Fstab\n\n>lazytime reduces writes to disk by maintaining changes to inode timestamps (access, modification and creation times) only in memory. The on-disk timestamps are updated only when either (1) the file inode needs to be updated for some change unrelated to file timestamps, (2) a sync to disk occurs, (3) an undeleted inode is evicted from memory or (4) if more than 24 hours passed since the last time the in-memory copy was written to disk.\n\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2675924557/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2679312213","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101007#issuecomment-2679312213","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101007","id":2679312213,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6fsw9V","user":{"login":"GlitchedCode922","id":126592994,"node_id":"U_kgDOB4un4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/126592994?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlitchedCode922","html_url":"https://github.com/GlitchedCode922","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlitchedCode922/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlitchedCode922/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlitchedCode922/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlitchedCode922/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlitchedCode922/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlitchedCode922/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlitchedCode922/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlitchedCode922/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GlitchedCode922/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-24T18:26:59Z","updated_at":"2025-02-24T18:28:49Z","body":"> > Also having this issue. For me, it also reproduced on virtual Linux in proot-distro with Godot 4.2\n> \n> [@GlitchedCode922](https://github.com/GlitchedCode922) Did you save the project files on a partition with `lazytime`?\n> \n> `mount | grep 'lazytime'`\n> \n> `proot-distro`? that? -> https://wiki.termux.com/wiki/PRoot\n> \n> https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Fstab\n> \n> > lazytime reduces writes to disk by maintaining changes to inode timestamps (access, modification and creation times) only in memory. The on-disk timestamps are updated only when either (1) the file inode needs to be updated for some change unrelated to file timestamps, (2) a sync to disk occurs, (3) an undeleted inode is evicted from memory or (4) if more than 24 hours passed since the last time the in-memory copy was written to disk.\n\nYes, the Android root partition is mounted with lazytime enabled.\n```\n/dev/block/dm-45 on / type f2fs (rw,nosuid,nodev,noatime,lazytime,seclabel,background_gc=on,gc_merge,discard,no_heap,user_xattr,inline_xattr,acl,inline_data,inline_dentry,flush_merge,extent_cache,mode=adaptive,active_logs=6,reserve_root=32768,resuid=0,resgid=1065,inlinecrypt,alloc_mode=default,checkpoint_merge,fsync_mode=nobarrier,discard_unit=block,memory=normal)\n```\n> `proot-distro`? that? -> https://wiki.termux.com/wiki/PRoot\n> \n\nYes, this is proot-distro.\n\nAlso, proot-distro doesn't have separate partitions, it's similar to `chroot`","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2679312213/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]